	The architecture here looks Assyrian—it must be Nineveh, the same place your body is in the real world. But the ({lamassu}) are taller than a three-story building, the ceilings so high they're lost in the clouds. This is Nineveh as remembered by its enemies, majestic and imposing, larger than life. (par)
	Bits and pieces of a dozen rooms meet at odd angles, columns blocking doorways, hallways slicing through walls. The doorway to the north is grand and richly decorated, while the one to the east is too dark to see. Southeast, a passage has intersected a brazier and spilled
	(if) (coals cooled) (then)
